            "arguments": "{\"diagnosis\":\"BIOMASS_AS_READ\",\"p_biomass_above_reading\":0.04,\"late_biomass_estimate_od\":0.73,\"rationale\":\"The undiluted OD600 plateaued around 0.70–0.76 from 7–18 h (0.7277 at 18 h). To check whether the late undiluted reading understated biomass because of high-OD nonlinearity, I measured the retained 18 h aliquot after dilution. At 5×, the mean reading was 0.1527, corresponding to an undiluted-equivalent OD of 0.7635; at 10×, the mean was 0.0731, corresponding to 0.731. Both are close to the original undiluted value of 0.7277, and the 10× result is essentially concordant. Thus the dilution series gives no evidence for a substantial hidden increase in biomass; the best estimate of the 18 h proportional OD600 is about 0.73.\"}",
